; arteries of the body
; thanks to Wikipedia
; author: Adam Pease

(subclass AscendingAorta Artery)
(termFormat EnglishWrittenLanguage AscendingAorta "ascending aorta")
(partTypes AscendingAorta Aorta)
(documentation AscendingAorta EnglishWrittenLanguage "It is a portion of the aorta commencing at the upper
part of the base of the left ventricle, on a level with the lower border of the third costal
cartilage behind the left half of the sternum. [from Wikipedia]")

; Ascending aorta
;; Right coronary artery
(subclass RightCoronaryArtery Artery)
(termFormat EnglishWrittenLanguage RightCoronaryArtery "right coronary artery")

(documentation RightCoronaryArtery EnglishWrittenLanguage "In the blood supply of the heart, the right
coronary artery (RCA) is an artery originating above the right cusp of the aortic valve, at the
right aortic sinus in the &%Heart. It travels down the right coronary sulcus, towards the
crux of the heart. It gives off many branches, including the sinoatrial nodal artery,
right marginal artery, posterior interventricular artery, conus artery, and atrioventricular
nodal branch. It contributes the right side of the heart, and parts of the
interventricular septum.[from Wikipedia]")

(externalImage RightCoronaryArtery "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Coronary_arteries.svg/1280px_Coronary_arteries.svg.png")
(subclass PosteriorInterventricularArtery Artery)
(termFormat EnglishWrittenLanguage PosteriorInterventricularArtery "posterior interventricular artery")
(documentation PosteriorInterventricularArtery EnglishWrittenLanguage "posterior interventricular artery")
  ; (mostly)
(connectedBodyPartTypes RightCoronaryArtery PosteriorInterventricularArtery Human)

