;; Left coronary artery
(subclass LeftCoronaryArtery Artery)
(termFormat EnglishWrittenLanguage LeftCoronaryArtery "left coronary artery")
(documentation LeftCoronaryArtery EnglishWrittenLanguage "The left coronary artery (LCA)
(also known as the left main coronary artery, or left main stem coronary artery)
is a coronary artery that arises from the aorta above the left cusp of the aortic
valve, and supplies blood to the left side of the heart muscle.
The left coronary artery typically runs for 10-25 mm, then bifurcates into the
left anterior descending artery, and the left circumflex artery.
The part that is between the aorta and the bifurcation only is known as the left
main artery (LM), while the term 'LCA' might refer to just the left main, or to
the left main and all its eventual branches.[from Wikipedia]")

(externalImage LeftCoronaryArtery "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Coronary_arteries.svg/1280px_Coronary_arteries.svg.png")
(connectedBodyPartTypes LeftCoronaryArtery AorticArch Human)

